 There are 13 ordered Android commands, exactly one fixed cmd package install -R -t --user 0 --pkg mutation. The others verify the commercial target, helper absence/identity or one state invocation. The helper must be absent for all users, including retained uninstalled records. The original action lock, once claim, worker budget, exact command policy, fresh APK hashes, state protocol, staging removal and FD/held cleanup remain. No automatic retry, uninstall, commercial launch, UI, settings, permissions or audio operation is provided.
 
 The actual six-value source assigns only this target's flow/state pair; all 913 prior values were excluded with one draw per label. Values are retained after any failure. Failed or uncertain installation requires durable-evidence reconciliation. Installation gives no business flow or whole-app qualification.
+
